{{/*
  ~/.tmux/plugins was tpm's install directory. tpm is gone — its two plugins
  were catppuccin, now written out inline in dot_tmux.conf, and
  vim-tmux-navigator, whose tmux half was never used. The rule stays as a guard:
  if a plugin manager is ever tried again, `chezmoi add` must not pull the tree
  in. It did once — 246 of the repo's 330 tracked files and 4.2MB were three
  vendored clones, .git directories and packfiles included — and beyond the bulk,
  chezmoi managing them means it fights the plugin manager on every update.
*/ -}}
.tmux/plugins/**

{{/*
  Machine-specific inclusion. This file is always evaluated as a template — no
  .tmpl suffix — so a path can be skipped per machine. Paths here are *target*
  names (.config/i3), not source names (dot_config/i3).

  i3 and i3status are the window manager and its status bar: Linux only. Only
  fontconfig looked like a candidate to join them, and it turns out to be
  present on macOS too.
*/ -}}
{{ if ne .chezmoi.os "linux" -}}
.config/i3/**
.config/i3status/**
{{ end -}}

{{/*
  The .spl beside the spell file is a build artifact: Neovim compiles it from
  en.utf-8.add and rewrites it whenever a word is added with zg. Tracking the
  source list is the point (config/options.lua explains why the path is set
  explicitly); tracking its compiled form would put a binary in the repo that
  goes stale the moment either machine learns a word. Ignored rather than merely
  left alone, because `chezmoi add ~/.config/nvim/spell` pulls it in otherwise —
  verified with --dry-run.
*/ -}}
.config/nvim/spell/*.spl

{{/*
  ~/.config/yazi/flavors and ~/.config/yazi/plugins are `ya pkg`'s install
  directories, the same relationship ~/.tmux/plugins has with tpm.
  package.toml *is* tracked — it records the flavor and the plugin and the
  commits they are pinned to, so `ya pkg install` reproduces both trees — but
  the fetched content is not, and is ignored here so `chezmoi add` cannot pull
  it in later.
*/ -}}
.config/yazi/flavors/**
.config/yazi/plugins/**

{{/*
  Karabiner-Elements is macOS-only. The profile it holds is the whole reason
  ctrl is reachable from both hands here — caps_lock and right_command both
  become control, and right_option becomes command so that hand keeps one too.
  Worth tracking precisely because nothing else in this repo can express it:
  kitty rejected the same remap outright (see dot_config/kitty/kitty.conf).

  Karabiner rewrites this file itself whenever the GUI changes a setting, the
  same two-writer situation as ~/.claude/settings.json — `chezmoi re-add` after
  changing anything in the app, or the next apply reverts it.
*/ -}}
{{ if ne .chezmoi.os "darwin" -}}
.config/karabiner/**
{{ end -}}

{{/*
  mkv2mp4 remuxes video and needs ffmpeg, which is a large install for a
  machine that is used for work. bootstrap.sh gates the ffmpeg package the same
  way, so the script and its dependency arrive together or not at all.
*/ -}}
{{ if ne .chezmoi.os "darwin" -}}
bin/mkv2mp4
{{ end -}}

{{/*
  ~/scratch holds the scratch notebooks — snacks writes them under opaque
  hashed names with a .meta sidecar, and they are working notes, not config.
  Only .prettierrc is tracked there, which sets the 100-column wrap those notes
  are formatted to (see config/scratch.lua for why it differs from the 120 the
  rest of the markdown here uses). Everything else is ignored so a
  `chezmoi add ~/scratch/...` cannot pull the notes in.
*/ -}}
scratch/*
!scratch/.prettierrc

